      "side": 1,
      "message": "It looks like this probably doesn\u0027t handle data limits and statistics correctly, due to trying to account the v4 clat+tether offloaded traffic against the v4- clat interface, instead of against the upstream cellular interface.\n\nI think we will need to teach the bpf program that it needs to do accounting against a different interface than the interface it redirects too.\n\nAdditionally it may need to account for the extra 20/28 byte clat overhead.\n\nLikely one (or more) of the existing bpf_tethering.h ipv4 maps needs to be extended with an extra interface index.\n\nie. perhaps Tether4Value {\n    uint32_t oif;             // The output interface to redirect to\n}\nneeds to gain a field:\n    uint32_t account_upstream_if;  // The output interface to redirect to\n\nAnd then if oif !\u003d account_upstream_if then you know 20/28 byte correction needs to happen.",
      "revId": "2e3aebefbff79209aa17e350bcd872ef3272a02b",
      "serverId": "85c56323-6fa9-3386-8a01-6480fb634889"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": false,
      "key": {
