      "writtenOn": "2022-11-25T08:06:24Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "This looks like it could be incorrect. AFAICT addUpstreamNameToLookupTable will ignore duplicate interface names and elements in that map are never deleted. But clatd interface names such as v4-wlan0 will have a different interface index every time clat is started.\n\nSo it looks like this code will only work the first time? Or am I missing something?\n\nWould it be correct to make addUpstreamNameToLookupTable *replace* the mapping every time a v4-xxx interface is added? Or does that information need to remain even after the interface gets deleted?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 1393,
        "startChar": 44,
        "endLine": 1393,
        "endChar": 72
      },
      "revId": "2e3aebefbff79209aa17e350bcd872ef3272a02b",
